The forked source lives under app/ and retains its Apache-2.0 licence; a copy
is at LICENSE-APACHE-2.0-buzz. Upstream publishes no NOTICE file of its own,
so nothing further is required to be reproduced here beyond this attribution.

What the fork changes, and why, is recorded in docs/BUZZ_FORK.md. The short
version: Buzz is a collaboration client, and AETHRION needs one. What AETHRION
additionally needs — that a message carries a declared type, that nothing said
in a channel can constitute a review, a verification or an acceptance — Buzz
does not have and was never trying to have. Those are added on top rather than
retrofitted into Buzz's own model, so that the fork can still take upstream
changes.
